A Body Blow? The War on Iran and U.S. Military Readiness <p>The war against Iran is putting new strains on U.S. military readiness by consuming munitions and missile defense interceptors, as well as through extended deployments, sustained operational demands, and the diversion of', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/a-body-blow-the-war-on-iran-and-u-s-military-readiness/'}, {'signal_id': 'cbccfe7292bfa507', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'An Army General Talks Fusing Sensors and Shooters on the Eastern Flank <p>This exclusive Cogs of War interview is with Brig. Gen. Steven P. Carpenter, the commanding general of Multi-Domain Command &#8211; Europe, the U.S. Army&#8217;s first multi-domain operations command, headq', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/an-army-general-talks-fusing-sensors-and-shooters-on-the-eastern-flank/'}, {'signal_id': '14613f43f63d6d48', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Real U.S.-Saudi Nuclear Deal Is Better Than We Thought <p>On Aug. 24, 2026, the Trump administration transmitted the text of the U.S.-Saudi nuclear cooperation agreement to Congress. By doing so, the administration triggered the 90-day congressional review process described i', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-real-u-s-saudi-nuclear-deal-is-better-than-we-thought/'}, {'signal_id': '1b6780d40e17f368', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Would NATO Membership for Ukraine Undermine Article 5 Itself? <p>In 2025, Jennifer Kavanaugh and Christopher McCallion wrote, &#8220;Armed Neutrality for Ukraine Is NATO&#8217;s Least Poor Option,&#8221; where they made the case for armed neutrality over full NATO membership as t', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/would-nato-membership-for-ukraine-undermine-article-5-itself/'}, {'signal_id': 'ba38c72ae33bc53d', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Strategic Stability and the Rebuilding of Xi’s Military <p>For all the warnings about an increasingly capable Chinese military, this may very well be an awkward moment for Beijing to have that military tested. General Secretary Xi Jinping has hollowed out much of the People&#8217', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/strategic-stability-and-the-rebuilding-of-xis-military/'}, {'signal_id': '331261e4ad7f06d4', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Atlantic Brief: U.S. and European Perspectives on Nuclear Deterrence <p>Date: Wednesday, Sept. 23, 2026Time: 12:00-1:00 PM ETThe second joint webinar by RUSI and War on the Rocks: Two leading defense publications from both sides of the Atlantic present their expert panel.&#16', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-atlantic-brief-u-s-and-european-perspectives-on-nuclear-deterrence/'}, {'signal_id': '0e3e84200aea153a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Three Patrons, Three Clients: The Mecca Alliance No One Owns <p>Every alliance contains a struggle over who gets to decide what the alliance is for. The unusual thing about the Mecca Alliance, formally known as the &#8220;Mecca Joint Defence Agreement,&#8221; is that all three of', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/three-patrons-three-clients-the-mecca-alliance-no-one-owns/'}, {'signal_id': '60d56685c2a1dbaa', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Reading the Kremlin’s Mind: Ukrainian Writers Attempt to Understand Putin <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated s', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/reading-the-kremlins-mind-ukrainian-writers-attempt-to-understand-putin/'}, {'signal_id': '5321bc66169b0448', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'This Is Not Your Father’s Nuclear Flight Test Vehicle <p>For decades, the United States&#8217; nuclear weapons enterprise has wrestled with an institutional paradox. On one hand is the imperative to make the complex more &#8220;responsive&#8221; to global tumult and technical sur', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/this-is-not-your-fathers-nuclear-flight-test-vehicle/'}, {'signal_id': '144f18951d48a536', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Big Bet on the Emerging Space Economy <p>The space economy has surpassed $600 billion in annual value, with some projecting it will reach a trillion by the 2030s. Jonathan Panter is joined by Joseph Yaffe (Cowboy Space), Brian Weeden (The Aerospace Corporation), and Dan Wald ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-big-bet-on-the-emerging-space-economy/'}, {'signal_id': '572beec097ba7921', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Age of Strategic Exclusion <p>Major powers are increasingly trying to shut out their rivals. Russia invaded Ukraine in part to prevent the latter&#8217;s further integration with the West. The United States is restricting China&#8217;s access to advanced semiconductors and en', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-age-of-strategic-exclusion/'}, {'signal_id': 'f0fc561dabb21987', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The War’s Last Generation Is Still Holding America’s Moral Debt <p>On the first night of the evacuation of Kabul, Aug. 15, 2021, a young mother found me in the crowd at Hamid Karzai International Airport. She had marked me, correctly, as someone who spoke her language. By the end', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-wars-last-generation-is-still-holding-americas-moral-debt/'}, {'signal_id': '4b88f91f1e94cc8a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'What America’s Adversaries and Allies Hope to Gain at the U.N. General Assembly <p>This year&#8217;s U.N. General Assembly officially opened on Tuesday, Sept. 8. The annual gathering gives diplomats and leaders a valuable opportunity to press their foreign policy priorities and e', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/what-americas-adversaries-and-allies-hope-to-gain-at-the-u-n-general-assembly/'}, {'signal_id': 'a7390c5588471bb5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Automating the Action Officer: Between Bureaucracy and Technology <p>If there is a revolution brewing in the automation of white-collar work, you wouldn&#8217;t know it at the Pentagon. Here, the typical action officers, staff who tackle the daily work of the bureaucracy, perform', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/automating-the-action-officer-between-bureaucracy-and-technology/'}, {'signal_id': '0b26e2a94a596635', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Assessment Gap in U.S. Counter-Terrorism Strikes <p>For eight years I helped decide whether American counter-terrorism money was working.As a programs advisor in the State Department&#8217;s Bureau of Counterterrorism from 2018 to 2025, I oversaw about 20 projects in East Afr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-assessment-gap-in-u-s-counter-terrorism-strikes/'}, {'signal_id': '2d8abdb2b2846625', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Forced Into the Right Decision? A Look at U.S. Land-Based Deterrence Posture <p>In 2019, Steve Fetter wrote &#8220;A Cheaper Nuclear Sponge,&#8221; in which he argued that building a new intercontinental ballistic missile (ICBM) was unnecessary for strengthening U.S. land-based d', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/forced-into-the-right-decision-a-look-at-u-s-land-based-deterrence-posture/'}, {'signal_id': 'cd0808c402ea03a0', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Tyranny of Shipyard Cost-Plus Contracting <p>As a naval shipyard commander, my mandate from Navy leadership is straightforward:&#160;return warships to the fleet as quickly as possible.&#160;Neither my shipyard nor many other public and private shipyards are consistently fulf', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-tyranny-of-shipyard-cost-plus-contracting/'}, {'signal_id': '1fa4ef77cf82cdeb', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Strange Transformation of the Front Line in Ukraine <p>On Jan. 5, 2025, my volunteer platoon attached to the 23rd Special Purpose Battalion of the Presidential Brigade entered a 1-kilometer-long tree line called CHAI, on the outskirts of Kotlyne, a few kilometers west of Pokr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-strange-transformation-of-the-front-line-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': '1670eaafeaf89241', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Mecca Pact’s Credibility Gap <p>Collective-defense pacts are meant to make war less likely. Poorly designed ones can do the opposite. If allies make sweeping promises without the military integration, decision-making mechanisms, and escalation controls needed to carry them ou', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-mecca-pacts-credibility-gap/'}, {'signal_id': '179f7c3bf766d1d7', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Two Questions Ukraine Asks Before Every Decision <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-two-questions-ukraine-asks-before-every-decision/'}, {'signal_id': '36101dbfb0e6fd00', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'China’s Warrior Scientists: Insights from Recent Operations Around Taiwan <p>China&#8217;s marine scientific research ships are expanding their operations around Taiwan, and they are not just there to advance the frontiers of human knowledge. Their operations serve to undermine T', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/chinas-warrior-scientists-insights-from-recent-operations-around-taiwan/'}, {'signal_id': '2e5e92fa8759b5b8', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Nicaragua’s Army Will Decide What Comes After Ortega <p>The first institution Nicaragua&#8217;s National Assembly called to testify on the constitutional reform ending competitive elections was the army. On July 29, 2026, Gen. Julio C&#233;sar Avil&#233;s appeared before the Spec', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/nicaraguas-army-will-decide-what-comes-after-ortega/'}, {'signal_id': 'fcd37ab58af255ca', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Strategic Fiber of America: Kevlar’s Impact on Warfighters <p>Editor&#8217;s note: This is the tenth and final article in a limited series celebrating American defense technologies born from wartime and their effects on broader national security, politics, and society. This s', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-strategic-fiber-of-america-kevlars-impact-on-warfighters/'}, {'signal_id': '39d9e910a88dec20', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Shrinking Buffers: Why Turkey and Israel Are on a Collision Course <p>When Israeli warplanes struck the Abu al-Duhur airbase in Syria on Aug. 18, 2026, the smoke rose over the demolition of an old geopolitical assumption about the Middle East. This time, Israel directly targeted ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/shrinking-buffers-why-turkey-and-israel-are-on-a-collision-course/'}, {'signal_id': 'ebe303df75565bf3', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'New Complications in Countering the Flow of Arms in the Caribbean <p>Arms trafficking in the Caribbean has soared in recent years, with many states now ranking firearms trafficking as the number one public safety and security threat. As new methods of arming individuals and gangs', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/new-complications-in-countering-the-flow-of-arms-in-the-caribbean/'}, {'signal_id': '562cfd567c178dd5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Fruit of Patience: How Regional Shifts Ripened Turkey’s Path to Kurdish Reconciliation <p>On Aug. 25, at the People&#8217;s Palace in Damascus, Mazloum Abdi announced the dissolution of the Syrian Democratic Forces, which he had commanded for a decade. Speaking first in Arabi', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-fruit-of-patience-how-regional-shifts-ripened-turkeys-path-to-kurdish-reconciliation/'}, {'signal_id': 'c5fd9481f083a76c', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Future of Combat Medicine <p>War has always been a brutal engine of medical innovation, running on a feedback loop: Civilian breakthroughs are adapted for the battlefield, while battlefield necessity pushes advances back into civilian care. We asked three experts to identify ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-future-of-combat-medicine/'}, {'signal_id': 'e5f45c9d96afca7a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Where Does AI Escalation Come From? We Don’t Know. We Should Find Out. <p>We played a wargame using AI players. Two nuclear-armed nations &#8212; Red and Blue &#8212; with a long-standing, fierce border dispute were placed into a militarized crisis. Over the course of several tur', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/where-does-ai-escalation-come-from-we-dont-know-we-should-find-out/'}, {'signal_id': 'ab358b5b30e1439a', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s Road to El Dorado <p>As a new convoy of Russian armored vehicles arrives from the port of Lom&#233; to support Russia&#8217;s Africa Corps deployment in Mali, that mission has entered its fifth year. Russia&#8217;s investment of blood and treasure urgently demands a retu', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/russias-road-to-el-dorado/'}, {'signal_id': '7fbe8eccdeb08001', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Is Taiwanese Society Prepared for a China Contingency? <p>In 2025, Michael Hunzeker and Yuster Yu wrote, &#8220;Taiwan&#8217;s Biggest Problem in Steeling Itself for War With China is Cultural,&#8221; where they argued major cultural changes were needed in both Taiwan&#8217;s mil', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/is-taiwanese-society-prepared-for-a-china-contingency/'}, {'signal_id': '079b19806a85db24', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'European Resilience in Digital Infrastructure: The Changing Nature of State-Business Relations <p>As the war in Ukraine progressed, Russian strikes increasingly degraded Ukraine&#8217;s terrestrial communications infrastructure, steadily deepening Kyiv&#8217;s dependence on Space', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/european-resilience-in-digital-infrastructure-the-changing-nature-of-state-business-relations/'}, {'signal_id': '735d938f937d5f34', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s Ground Robots and the Economics of Survival <p>In August 2024, special forces from five Ukrainian military intelligence units crossed the Black Sea to raid Russian-held Kinburn Spit. The commandos of these units &#8212; Chimera, Aratta, Stuhna, Paragon, Terror, and the ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/ukraines-ground-robots-and-the-economics-of-survival/'}, {'signal_id': 'd334c7e095244b24', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Why Are People Talking About a German Reset with Russia? <p>The summer of 2026 has raised questions once again among politicians, diplomats, and academics about whether Germany might be about to dither on Russia. Last month, a drone attack on German soil seemed designed to coerce', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/why-are-people-talking-about-a-german-reset-with-russia/'}, {'signal_id': 'e2d349353aa76edc', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'A Rulebook for Surprises: Commanding Autonomous Aircraft <p>My greatest challenge while flight testing collaborative combat aircraft was not troubleshooting errors at high speed in the cockpit. It was when, in a single keystroke, my job shifted from pilot to something like a dog ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/a-rulebook-for-surprises-commanding-autonomous-aircraft/'}, {'signal_id': '9d158e146afea4cd', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Educated Operator: Rethinking Lethality in Special Operations <p>Editor&#8217;s Note: While War on the Rocks has a high standard for allowing pseudonyms, this is an unusual case: U.S. Army Special Operations Command requires its uniformed personnel to use pseudonyms when writ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-educated-operator-rethinking-lethality-in-special-operations/'}, {'signal_id': '373c93386053b689', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Political Constraint on America’s Data-Center Power Buildout <p>In April, President Donald Trump issued two Defense Production Act determinations covering grid infrastructure and large-scale energy infrastructure. One found that the country&#8217;s constrained electric grid p', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-political-constraint-on-americas-data-center-power-buildout/'}, {'signal_id': '4f42f3d54707c448', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Divine Calculus of the Ukraine War’s End <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles from Ukr', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-divine-calculus-of-the-ukraine-wars-end/'}, {'signal_id': '0c59bb2905c426b5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Quantum Stack and the Countdown to Q-Day <p>Quantum&#8217;s hype obscures a reality with real geopolitical stakes: the technology works and is advancing every day. Cameron Chehreh (IonQ), JD Dulny (Booz Allen), and Ben Gianni (GDIT) join Jonathan to discuss the race to Q-Day.', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-quantum-stack-and-the-countdown-to-q-day/'}, {'signal_id': '880faa7eae8f8153', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Stop Using AI. Start Commanding It <p>Walk into the Pentagon, climb the escalator, and an Uncle Sam-style poster points at you: &#8220;I want YOU to use AI.&#8221; It worked. GenAI.mil hit 1.5 million users in six months, and I have heard enough OpenAI-in-disguise pitches to last', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/stop-using-ai-start-commanding-it/'}, {'signal_id': 'aec0b7a6b34cfdc5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The (Un)importance of the Battle of Tours <p>Editor&#8217;s note: This is the first article in a new occasional series featuring battles that just didn&#8217;t matter, may look important, but in fact had negligible strategic or political effects or were absurd, anticlimactic, or ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-unimportance-of-the-battle-of-tours/'}, {'signal_id': '2ec963079b886612', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Beneath the Surface: Overlooked Cyber Security Threats <p>Cyber security remains a persistent concern for public and private sector organizations alike. Given the potential impact of cyber threats from criminal groups, adversarial states, and extremists, the topic draws substanti', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/beneath-the-surface-overlooked-cyber-security-threats/'}, {'signal_id': '129f309bfa610424', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Goldilocks Fallacy: The Undefined Limits of Korea’s Nuclear Role <p>&#8220;Unthreatening and respectful.&#8221; That is how the president of the United States described North Korea on Aug. 16, 2026, in his social media post ordering his secretary of defense to scale back join', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-goldilocks-fallacy-the-undefined-limits-of-koreas-nuclear-role/'}, {'signal_id': '8636b32c16738d4f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': '“Zero Problems” Abroad, Plenty at Home: Reassessing al Sharaa’s Leadership in Syria <p>In 2025, Rob Geist Pinfold wrote, &#8220;The March Massacres Show That Syria Urgently Needs Solutions, Not Sanctions,&#8221; in which he argued that sanctions relief was a major way the West co', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/zero-problems-abroad-plenty-at-home-reassessing-al-sharaas-leadership-in-syria/'}, {'signal_id': 'b91f521bf75c15d8', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Marine Corps’ Plan for the Future of Ground Combat <p>The Marine Corps just released its plan to fight against adversaries on land, and Ryan had the two architects of the plan, Ground Combat Element 2040, on the show to talk about it. They discuss drones, resilience, long-ran', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-marine-corps-plan-for-the-future-of-ground-combat/'}, {'signal_id': '66de9a287b9f7b96', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Would Wartime Elections Save Democracy or End It? <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of articles fro', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/would-wartime-elections-save-democracy-or-end-it/'}, {'signal_id': '47b3384c86979a8d', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'From Hormuz to the Caucasus: The New Geography of Energy Security <p>Every crisis in the Middle East returns the world&#8217;s attention to the same stretch of water. When tankers are seized, or missiles fly near the Persian Gulf, oil prices move, insurers reprice risk, shipping ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/from-hormuz-to-the-caucasus-the-new-geography-of-energy-security/'}, {'signal_id': 'f1a52f2f9b27d6d9', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Russia’s Next Top General: Promotions in Russian Military Leadership <p>Judged by the initial strategic goals set by Russian President Vladimir Putin in 2022, Russia&#8217;s military lost its war against Ukraine some time ago. Yet Russia&#8217;s armed forces have not stopped figh', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/russias-next-top-general-promotions-in-russian-military-leadership/'}, {'signal_id': '0414e38a05ab0848', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Command and Politics in the War Between Moscow and Kyiv <p>Our intrepid team covers a lot of ground in this episode: the increasing fluidity of the battlefield, drones and air defense, the biting Black Sea campaign, the causes and aftermath of the firing of Ukraine&#8217;s popula', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/command-and-politics-in-the-war-between-moscow-and-kyiv/'}, {'signal_id': 'abd707fb2ab0d396', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Betting on Autonomous Aircraft <p>This exclusive Cogs of War interview is with Brandon Tseng, the co-founder and president of Shield AI and a former Navy SEAL, whose company builds the Hivemind autonomy software, the V-BAT and X-BAT aircraft, and Aechelon synthetic reality and si', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/betting-on-autonomous-aircraft/'}, {'signal_id': 'd71e5526eed91ab0', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Risks of Downplaying China’s Military <p>China has spent years modifying civilian ferries to launch amphibious armored vehicles, developing specialized equipment to move forces ashore without conventional port facilities, hardening dozens of air bases, and rapidly expanding t', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-risks-of-downplaying-chinas-military/'}, {'signal_id': '8495954fd84049f6', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Pressure Points: Economic Strain, Allied Discord, and War Fatigue <p>Welcome to The Adversarial.&#160;Every other week, we&#8217;ll provide you with expert analysis on America&#8217;s greatest challengers: China, Russia, Iran, North Korea, and jihadists. Read more below.***IranU.', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/pressure-points-economic-strain-allied-discord-and-war-fatigue/'}, {'signal_id': '9b99a84b384ff5bc', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'A Rock and China’s Three-Sea Problem <p>Two rocks surrounded by coral, with a total land size of less than 10 square meters (approximately 108 square feet) at high tide, are the entire basis on which Japan claims a 150,000-square-mile exclusive economic zone, an area nearly the s', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/a-rock-and-chinas-three-sea-problem/'}, {'signal_id': 'f1e64957581cf27d', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Mental Health Is a Warfighting Readiness Problem for the U.S. Navy <p>&#8220;You cannot be at mental peace always. You will be worried. So even my family &#8212; they are scared all the time, and they were anxiously praying [for] the vessel [to] come out of this area safely.&#822', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/mental-health-is-a-warfighting-readiness-problem-for-the-u-s-navy/'}, {'signal_id': '5b7e7cad88ee8129', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'War: Watt Is It Good For? <p>Military analysts are captivated by how the material nature of war is transforming in Ukraine. Unmanned systems have captured Russian infantry units, battered Russian naval and commercial ships, and even, with the help of on-board AI, conducted autono', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/war-watt-is-it-good-for/'}, {'signal_id': '118d32c332b0f08b', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'China’s Military Says AI Can’t Replace Commanders. Xi Is Testing That <p>For years, the Chinese military&#8217;s own newspaper has been making a promise it may no longer be able to keep. Whenever the People&#8217;s Liberation Army Daily (Jiefangjun Bao), the official newspaper of', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/chinas-military-says-ai-cant-replace-commanders-xi-is-testing-that/'}, {'signal_id': 'd1fe84899d9acbcc', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Inside Iran’s Wartime Regime <p>Afshon Ostovar, one of the leading experts on Iran and the host of the members-only podcast The Iran Reckoning, is joined by War on the Rocks membership editor Kerry Anderson for a state-of-play conversation on the conflict between the United State', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/inside-irans-wartime-regime/'}, {'signal_id': '30c28f7be4336ab5', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Contested Logistics and the “Last Unmanned Mile” <p>In a Pacific war, the U.S. military cannot assume uncontested access to its depots and supply lines for munitions, spare parts, food, water, and energy. Jonathan is joined by David Tuttle (Rune Technologies), Paul Lwin (HavocAI)', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/contested-logistics-and-the-last-unmanned-mile/'}, {'signal_id': 'dde294cf53e0ce48', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Managed Instability: Why the Wars Against Iran and Ukraine Can Go On and On and On… <p>The Iran war is beginning to resemble the Ukraine war in one important way. Operationally, the wars themselves are still very different &#8212; Ukraine is a large-scale ground invasion, while t', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/managed-instability-why-the-wars-against-iran-and-ukraine-can-go-on-and-on-and-on/'}, {'signal_id': '536eed887a46bd73', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Proving the Negative: Three Warnings from Arms Control for the Age of AI <p>In early 1963, a single number characterized the difference in the positions of the United States and the Soviet Union on a comprehensive nuclear test ban. Nikita Khrushchev had proposed three on-site ins', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/proving-the-negative-three-warnings-from-arms-control-for-the-age-of-ai/'}, {'signal_id': 'c84c59612f46ef45', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'How Feasible Is a European Nuclear Deterrent Without Washington? <p>In 2025, James Cameron wrote, &#8220;Eurodeterrent: A Vision for an Anglo-French Nuclear Force,&#8221; where he argued the United Kingdom and France should cooperate to develop a nuclear deterrent umbrella for Eu', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/how-feasible-is-a-european-nuclear-deterrent-without-washington/'}, {'signal_id': 'a222ab451bad7e8f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'AI and the Risks of Tearing Down an Old System <p>Operation Epic Fury made clear that AI is now at the heart of American warfighting. Central Command used Claude through Palantir&#8217;s Maven Smart System platform to generate and prioritize roughly 1,000 targets in the first 24 ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/ai-and-the-risks-of-tearing-down-an-old-system/'}, {'signal_id': '0b7dabf96e698b4b', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Inside Brazil’s 3D-Printed Gun Supply Chain <p>On June 26, 2026, the Civil Police of Rio de Janeiro, through its specialized firearms, ammunition, and explosives unit, raided a clandestine workshop in Rio das Pedras, on the city&#8217;s west side. Investigators said the group use', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/inside-brazils-3d-printed-gun-supply-chain/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4240b5af49a1b0e', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Tension Between Collectivism and Individualism in Ukraine <p>Welcome to&#160;The Ukraine Compass, a weekly digest of Ukrainian commentary and analysis from across the political spectrum, only for War on the Rocks&#160;members. Each Monday, we bring you a curated selection of ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-tension-between-collectivism-and-individualism-in-ukraine/'}, {'signal_id': 'de413bd418f249d9', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'A Life in Army Special Operations, from Desert Storm to the Next War <p>Lt. Gen. (ret.) Francis Beaudette, former commanding general of the U.S. Army Special Operations Command, joins Ryan to discuss how his family history, service, and books shaped his path into and time in the ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/a-life-in-army-special-operations-from-desert-storm-to-the-next-war/'}, {'signal_id': '1c913ee918631745', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Blanchard’s Lathe and the Long Arc of American Manufacturing <p>Editor&#8217;s note: This is the ninth article in a limited series celebrating American defense technologies born from wartime and their effects on broader national security, politics, and society. This series will r', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/blanchards-lathe-and-the-long-arc-of-american-manufacturing/'}, {'signal_id': '7001cb62dd3ad80f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'What Have We Learned from the 9/11 Wars? Not Nearly Enough <p>Editor&#8217;s Note: The following article draws on themes from the author&#8217;s forthcoming book titled US Counterterrorism Operations in Afghanistan: Jackpots, Dry Holes, and Collateral Damage.Over the next month, ', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/what-have-we-learned-from-the-9-11-wars-not-nearly-enough/'}, {'signal_id': 'c4e99b7238b2753f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'Cheap Drones, Dry Taps: The Iran War Opens a New Era of Water Infrastructure Risk <p>Water and energy infrastructure have become one of Iran&#8217;s main levers of deterrence against the United States. Iranian Foreign Minister Aragchi recently made it clear to Gulf states that if', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cheap-drones-dry-taps-the-iran-war-opens-a-new-era-of-water-infrastructure-risk/'}, {'signal_id': '3a54e85ac26dd829', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The Commercial Space Race <p>A strong commercial space industry is an important partner for the U.S. government, as it contributes to building more robust space and defense capabilities and facilitates innovation more broadly. As competition between the United States and China he', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/the-commercial-space-race/'}, {'signal_id': '27c7f2e427dedd1f', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': 'The True Cost of Cheap Chips <p>Given the relentless demand for computing power, electronic components are in scarce supply. Prices for certain memory chips, known as DRAM, have surged by more than 50 percent in a single quarter this year, and have roughly quadrupled since last f', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/cogs-of-war/the-true-cost-of-cheap-chips/'}, {'signal_id': '8f00ca4743ace463', 'source': 'war_on_the_rocks', 'text_snippet': '2026 and All That: Another Benchmark Year in Royal Navy Decline <p>The 1930 comic history, 1066 and All That, made famous the British habit of reducing national history to a sequence of memorable dates. The modern Royal Navy has its own unhappy version of that calendar. Since 194', 'url': 'https://warontherocks.com/2026-and-all-that-another-benchmark-year-in-royal-navy-decline/'}, {'signal_id': 'cd18ee2f4feb9892', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Iran Calls Itself the Victim, Its Record Tells Another Story <p>Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian’s speech at the United Nations did not mention Iran’s history of terrorism and the thousands of innocent victims killed, or the imprisonment and killing of thousands of its own peo', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/iran-calls-itself-the-victim-its-record-tells-another-story'}, {'signal_id': '63a09464be695214', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Exactly how could AI kill humans? <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/us-united-nations-ai.jpg?id=68021413&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordinates=0%2C53%2C0%2C54" /><br /><br /><p>Nobel laureate Geoffrey Hinton walked out of a closed-door Capitol Hill br', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/exactly-how-could-ai-kill-humans'}, {'signal_id': '6312ebc7e719c5db', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Nasrallah is Dead. Hezbollah’s Social Lifeline is Not. <p>Two years after Israel <a href="https://www.idf.il/310591" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">killed</a> Hassan Nasrallah, Hezbollah is weaker but not finished. WaTaawanou, a crowdfunded charity outside Hezbollah’s ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/nasrallah-is-dead-hezbollahs-social-lifeline-is-not'}, {'signal_id': '232d9c460397b23a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'BLUF: Russian Strategic Culture Drives its Callous and Brutal Actions <p>My friends and family often ask me why Russia behaves so offensively. They are baffled by Russia’s lack of humanity and Moscow’s actions such as hiring assassins, launching drones at innocents, and planning ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/bluf-russian-strategic-culture-drives-its-callous-and-brutal-actions'}, {'signal_id': '19486bf2eea53f8a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How the Intelligence Community Can Shape AI Trust With New Terminology <p><strong><em>The Intelligence Community (IC) has an opportunity now to influence how we talk about, and thus how we approach, AI use in our work by formally adopting the nomenclature “AI-in-the-Loop” rather ', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-the-intelligence-community-can-shape-ai-trust-with-new-terminology'}, {'signal_id': '55054f1ba5989102', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Coupang Breach and the Danger of Punishing the Headline Number <p>The headline number from the Coupang data breach — <a href="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c36zwywll02o" target="_blank" title="https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c36zwywll02o"><u>more than 33 million user ac', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-coupang-breach-and-the-danger-of-punishing-the-headline-number'}, {'signal_id': '7bcfc9e11fa2d866', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Houthis Took the Red Sea Coast. How Did Washington Miss It? <p>The recent military moves taken by Yemens Houthis resulted in <strong>stunning victories and significant strategic gains,</strong> virtually unopposed. By taking the Red Sea port of Mocha (Al-Makha), occupying Per', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-houthis-took-the-red-sea-coast-how-did-washington-miss-it'}, {'signal_id': '23f20cc3fe6cfc2a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'AI Is Coming to the Counter-Drone Fight <p>“Twenty years ago, the state of North Dakota poured in multiple millions of dollars to figure out what it looks like to do beyond visual line-of-sight operations for Class One, Two, and Three Drones. That was just the very nascent stage.', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/ai-is-coming-to-the-counter-drone-fight'}, {'signal_id': 'ef1a257a183f79d5', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Trump’s Rejection of Iran Offer Highlights Another Big Problem <p>Beijing says artificial intelligence will give the state a visible hand to allocate capital. Here’s the rub: Washington’s economic authority sits in five places, and none of them is in command.</p><div class="horiz', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/trumps-rejection-of-iran-offer-highlights-another-big-problem'}, {'signal_id': '4cafdaacc91eb924', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'NATO Can’t Count Its Way to Maritime Superiority <p>Allied navies are still counting hulls. The contest at sea is now about who sees, decides, and acts first.</p><p>Earlier this month, Western officials <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/nato-allies-foil-russian-subsea', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/nato-cant-count-its-way-to-maritime-superiority'}, {'signal_id': '6159fff54410155c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Iran’s Regime Is Weaker Than It Looks <p>For five and a half years, I was a hostage of the Islamic Republic of Iran. During that time, I came to believe something about the regime that may seem improbable from the outside: It is far weaker than it looks. Today, I believe we are c', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/irans-regime-is-weaker-than-it-looks'}, {'signal_id': '7fb68a7caf5acda9', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'A warning about ‘model welfare’ <p><a href="https://mustafa-suleyman.ai/claudes-constitution-highlighted.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Download a highlighted marked-up version of the Claude Constitution</a><br /><a href="https://mustafa-suleyman.ai/ModelWelfare_T', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/a-warning-about-model-welfare'}, {'signal_id': '4a03c7a9df58f5d3', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Navigating a More Uncertain World: Lessons from CIA’s Red Cell <p>Twenty-five years after 9/11, the United States is confronting yet another era of profound uncertainty and potential dangers. The pace and scale of change are creating unforeseen disruptions that impact our securit', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/navigating-a-more-uncertain-world-lessons-from-cias-red-cell'}, {'signal_id': '57581444e897d39c', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'When Threats Move Faster Than Institutions <p>A major aspect of the national security story of the past year comes down to one gap. Our adversaries, and increasingly the machines they use, now operate at machine speed. The institutions we count on for defense, oversight, and trus', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/when-threats-move-faster-than-institutions'}, {'signal_id': '91e346a8595311a4', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'AI Is Coming for the Chain of Command <p>The voice belonged to Gen. Tareq Saleh. It was telling his men to fall back. Or so it seemed.</p><p><em>“Advances and retreats are a normal part of war,”</em> the recording reasoned. <em>“Pull back toward Mocha.”</em></p><p>It was mid-Sept', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/ai-is-coming-for-the-chain-of-command'}, {'signal_id': 'f4a082ed4a47127a', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Putin Is Testing the West’s Resolve <p>In the preface to volume one, “The Gathering Storm,” of his six-volume memoir of World War II, British Prime Minister Winston Churchill recalls a conversation with U.S. President Franklin Roosevelt, in which Roosevelt asked what the war shou', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/putin-is-testing-the-wests-resolve'}, {'signal_id': '4ba387c4d355cdf5', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Nations That Don’t Appear on the Map <p>The most influential media network operating inside a dozen allied countries today has no masthead, no headquarters and no country of incorporation. It has roughly 50 million members across more than 150 countries. It is the Chinese dia', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-nations-that-dont-appear-on-the-map'}, {'signal_id': 'd73541cee321794b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Military’s Race to Operationalize AI <p>“I feel as though I was catapulted into a dystopian future in which the battlefield (or ‘kill zone’ as Ukrainians call it) is dominated by drones and sensors, and will increasingly be shaped by AI [Artificial Intelligence], too. It’s wh', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-militarys-race-to-operationalize-ai'}, {'signal_id': 'c15da364fc3b9a3e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Authority We Cannot Keep <p>Washington announced permanent control of Greenland on Friday. The two governments that must ratify it announced, in the same breath, that the text recognizes their sovereignty. Both ideas cannot be the settled meaning of an agreement neither parli', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-authority-we-cannot-keep'}, {'signal_id': 'f386748fccb2924b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "Heads They Win, Tails They Win: The CMMC Trap and the Way Out <p>Here is a prediction from inside the compliance trenches: the CMMC Reform Task Force closed its sixty-day review on September 11 and is now finalizing recommendations for the Department of War's Chief Information Of", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/heads-they-win-tails-they-win-the-cmmc-trap-and-the-way-out-2677900776'}, {'signal_id': '337b2e9db980b1f3', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How America Appeased Putin <img src="https://www.thecipherbrief.com/media-library/moscow-kremlin-stock-photo.jpg?id=67792957&amp;width=1245&amp;height=700&amp;coordinates=0%2C261%2C0%2C261" /><br /><br /><p><em>Excerpt from Spies: The Epic Intelligence War Between East and West</', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-america-appeased-putin'}, {'signal_id': '08cad92585a0e2b3', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Will Physical AI Underpin the Reindustrialization Win that Western Allies Need? <p>Having spent most of my life working in “advanced nations” that have strategically accentuated financial and professional services growth while outsourcing manufacturing to the lowest cost jurisdic', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/will-physical-ai-underpin-the-reindustrialization-win-that-western-allies-need'}, {'signal_id': '33cc559b775f0bf9', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'How China Is Building an Architecture of Control Across the Heart of Asia <p>In the years following the Soviet withdrawal from Afghanistan, much of the world treated the region as strategically peripheral - unstable, exhausted, and largely disconnected from the future of global s', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/how-china-is-building-an-architecture-of-control-across-the-heart-of-asia'}, {'signal_id': '22baf55102af104b', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Dark Transits are a Stopgap not a Solution <p>Washington has accomplished an important feat by stealthily moving oil through the Persian Gulf despite Iran’s proclaimed closure. But the means it has relied on can’t become normal maritime behavior.</p><p>Treasury Secretary Scott Be', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/dark-transits-are-a-stopgap-not-a-solution'}, {'signal_id': '848749d86e14463e', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Houthis’ Coastal Gambit <p>For the first time in years, large swaths of Yemeni territory are changing hands. The Houthis’ recent losses in the east of the country were quickly followed by a string of victories along the Red Sea coast that brought the group closer to the Bab a', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-houthis-coastal-gambit'}, {'signal_id': 'f8815d28c73b6165', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': '65 Billion Barrels Is Only the Beginning <p>President Trump announced this weekend that the United States had secured majority control over more than 65 billion barrels of Venezuela’s proven oil reserves through a partnership with private business.</p><p>That is a big number. But', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/65-billion-barrels-is-only-the-beginning'}, {'signal_id': '48ce5508730034f3', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'The Bells are Ringing Again, and This Time Sweden is Inside the Alliance <p>On August 25, <a href="https://www.cnn.com/2026/08/27/politics/john-ratcliffe-cia-moscow-visit" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CIA Director John Ratcliffe landed in Moscow</a>. He met Russian o', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/the-bells-are-ringing-again-and-this-time-sweden-is-inside-the-alliance'}, {'signal_id': '4d3551811260a516', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'We Are In An Unpredictable War Of Attrition <p><strong><em>We are squarely in the target sights of ‘Unintended Consequences.’</em></strong></p><p>What do I mean by this? Think of it as a broad spectrum of possible consequences when missiles and drones are being slung back and for', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/we-are-in-an-unpredictable-war-of-attrition'}, {'signal_id': 'ffcb69390d2c5b25', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': "Can America’s All-Volunteer Force Survive the Next War? <p>“It made sense for the United States to transition from this mixed force of conscripts and professionals to an All-Volunteer Force. It has enabled us to develop a truly professionalized force. It's a professionalized forc", 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/can-americas-all-volunteer-force-survive-the-next-war'}, {'signal_id': 'c490ad47f23d7c06', 'source': 'cipher_brief', 'text_snippet': 'Setting Terms with America’s Tech Giants <p>If China attacked Taiwan tomorrow, the question might not be which aircraft carrier sails first to the Pacific, but whether a private company will activate satellite coverage over a small island. As Ukraine does today, Taiwan could soon', 'url': 'https://www.thecipherbrief.com/setting-terms-with-americas-tech-giants'}, {'signal_id': '3d3d1b48ab5ce092', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Under the Gaza Peace Plan, Who Is Responsible for the Treatment of Protected Persons and What Does That Require? <p>An analysis of the obligations that the Board of Peace and International Stabilization Force must fulfill with respect to the civilian population of Gaza.</p>\n<p>Th', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/158970/gaza-peace-plan-who-responsible-protected-persons/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=gaza-peace-plan-who-responsible-protected-persons'}, {'signal_id': '0889ea05bbca651e', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: October 2, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR Senior Iranian commanders are reviewing plans to expand potential targets beyond', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159499/early-edition-october-2-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-october-2-2026'}, {'signal_id': '42bffd115e669f99', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'The Just Security Podcast: What Happened at the 2026 UN General Assembly? <p>Daniel Forti and Mariea Sekijima join Viola Gienger to discuss the most important developments from the 2026 UN General Assembly.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/159392/just-securit', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159392/just-security-podcast-2026-un-general-assembly/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=just-security-podcast-2026-un-general-assembly'}, {'signal_id': '0a246c18980d7e69', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': "Activists at the Poland-Belarus Border are Still Being Prosecuted for Providing Aid to Migrants <p>People who help migrants and asylum seekers at Poland's border with Belarus continue to be targeted with prosecutions, interrogations, and home searches by Polish authorities.</p>\n<", 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159248/poland-belarus-border-migrants-activists-prosecuted/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=poland-belarus-border-migrants-activists-prosecuted'}, {'signal_id': '03363f5eaf66d5e7', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Dangerous Warning Signs from the First-Ever ATRC Case <p>The first-ever case brought before the Alien Terrorist Removal Court displayed the dangers the court poses to democratic rights.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/159035/dangerous-warning-signs-first-atr', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159035/dangerous-warning-signs-first-atrc-case/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=dangerous-warning-signs-first-atrc-case'}, {'signal_id': 'ca9c59328672ecb7', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'How Will Congress and the Public Learn the Details of Trump’s Venezuela Oil Deal? <p>If the Trump administration declines to disclose the terms of the Venezuela oil deal, Congress has tools available to compel it to do so.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/159', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159351/how-will-congress-public-learn-trump-venezuela-oil-deal/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=how-will-congress-public-learn-trump-venezuela-oil-deal'}, {'signal_id': '2832e19fda8bc4d9', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Early Edition: October 1, 2026 <p>Sign up to receive the Early Edition in your inbox\xa0here. A curated weekday guide to major news and developments over the last 24 hours. Here’s today’s news: IRAN WAR U.S. Secretary of State Marco Rubio on Monday demanded the Iranian delegation to', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159415/early-edition-october-1-2026/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=early-edition-october-1-2026'}, {'signal_id': '71251dc4c0815961', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Litigation Tracker: Legal Challenges to Trump Administration Actions <p>A public resource tracking all the legal challenges to the Trump administration\'s executive orders and actions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/107087/tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tracker-litigation-legal-challenges-trump-administration'}, {'signal_id': '6515fcd8636ec9fc', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Guantanamo Dispatch: Military Ends USS Cole Hearing Early for Health Emergency <p>Pretrial hearings in the USS Cole bombing case ended abruptly on Wednesday after the case\'s death-penalty defense lawyer had a health emergency.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/159334/guantanamo-dispatch-military-ends-uss-cole-hearing-early-for-health-emergency/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=guantanamo-dispatch-military-ends-uss-cole-hearing-early-for-health-emergency'}, {'signal_id': '9aeb621835f53761', 'source': 'just_security', 'text_snippet': 'Standing Up for International Law <p>When academics, business and law firm heads, and leaders of international associations like the ABILA defend the rule of law, those ripples can build into a wave of change.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.justsecurity.org/157833/standing-', 'url': 'https://www.justsecurity.org/157833/standing-up-for-international-law/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=standing-up-for-international-law'}, {'signal_id': '510596eafa31042f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'From Strategic Logic to Practical Implementation: A Phased Agenda for U.S.-ROK Shipbuilding Cooperation U.S.-ROK cooperation on shipbuilding should be structured so that it strengthens U.S. maritime industrial capacity, makes commercial sense for Korean shipbuilders, and survives', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/from-strategic-logic-to-practical-implementation-a.html'}, {'signal_id': 'c5904b48ce512115', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "9/11's Forgotten Lesson Twenty-five years later, 9/11's lessons are still contested, except the simplest: the United States mistook quiet for peace. And it is doing so again.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/10/911s-forgotten-lesson.html'}, {'signal_id': '645e5c8159c45b3c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Schools, Cell Phones, and AI: Q&amp;A with Melissa Kay Diliberti Melissa Kay Diliberti, an associate policy researcher at RAND, discusses recent findings from RAND that can help parents and policymakers better understand what challenges schools are up against.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/schools-cell-phones-and-ai-qa-with-melissa-kay-diliberti.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f0a6bf01926bc40a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Netanyahu May Have Ignored a Dire Warning. Israel Ignores the Deeper Threat. Israel's strategy in Gaza is only keeping Hamas in power: deterred, but not replaced, with no real alternative given a chance. A different outcome calls for a different approach.", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/nentanyahu-may-have-ignored-a-dire-warning-israel-ignores-the.html'}, {'signal_id': 'b489a15858be84c1', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Never Underestimate the Houthis Yemen's Houthi rebels are in a position to shape the next phase of the conflict between the United States and Iran if they attempt to renew their blockade of the Bab al-Mandab Strait. And no one should assume that a deal with Iran will bind what th", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/never-underestimate-the-houthis.html'}, {'signal_id': '19d8064c433770cf', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Preserving Jobs and Tax Revenue in the Age of AI: Q&amp;A with Carter Price Carter Price, a mathematician at RAND and co-director of the RAND Von Furstenberg Family Budget Model Initiative, discusses ways to rebalance the tax code so that it doesn't incentivize employers to repla", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/preserving-jobs-and-tax-revenue-in-the-age-of-ai-qa.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2d02311d1d9e0e7', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The Recent Rise of Women Gun Owners In recent years, women made up almost half of all new gun owners, a striking shift from the historical norm, when women accounted for about a quarter of them. And the uptick is widespread across geographic and demographic subgroups.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/the-recent-rise-of-women-gun-owners.html'}, {'signal_id': '2a9dc8988cf7146c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Who Benefits from Education Savings Accounts? Q&amp;A with Susha Roy Tens of thousands of American families use state-funded education savings accounts for their children's education. How exactly do these accounts work? Who benefits from them? And how do they affect education fun", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/who-benefits-from-education-savings-accounts.html'}, {'signal_id': '480b7da85115059d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Getting a Security Clearance Doesn't Have to Be So Intimidating: Q&amp;A with Sina Beaghley The security clearance process can be difficult and time-consuming but the government has made big strides in improving it. Sina Beaghley, a senior international and defense researcher at ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/getting-a-security-clearance-doesnt-have-to-be-so-intimidating.html'}, {'signal_id': 'd2b8719ed5ca0a96', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': '25 Years After 9/11: Lessons for Securing the Homeland Reflecting on 25 years since the September 11 terror attacks, RAND experts answer questions about protecting soft targets, the role of the TSA, mitigating risks from emerging technologies, and more.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/25-years-after-911-lessons-for-securing-the-homeland.html'}, {'signal_id': '080553cfaf2bb84f', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'AI Can Now Design Viruses. We Need Biosecurity Guardrails Now As AI advances, the risk of engineered viral bioweapons is growing. The window to prepare is now—by building a layered, resilient system of defense.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/ai-can-now-design-viruses-we-need-biosecurity-guardrails.html'}, {'signal_id': '20bc7f624125f201', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Tomorrow's Victory and the Army of the Future: Forecasting the Next Steps in Ukraine's Military Evolution Ukraine’s military has changed substantially since Russia’s full-scale invasion in 2022. Will its next evolution be shaped by traditionalists or technologists?", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/tomorrows-victory-and-the-army-of-the-future.html'}, {'signal_id': 'f540d78c60af3817', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'When Disaster Strikes, Could AI Help? Q&amp;A with Jessica Jensen Disasters are more frequent, more severe, and more costly. Pressure is mounting on emergency managers and the organizations that support them. Senior policy researcher Jessica Jensen discusses how artificial intell', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/09/when-disaster-strikes-could-ai-help-qa-with-jessica.html'}, {'signal_id': '1661e5b81ca5f2ab', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Not All ‘Magic’ Mushrooms Are the Same Millions of U.S. adults use <em>Amanita muscaria</em> mushrooms. But these distinctive fungi aren’t like other psychoactive mushrooms. What do consumers and policymakers need to know about them?', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/not-all-magic-mushrooms-are-the-same.html'}, {'signal_id': '9e7a1d6837563ea8', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "Mirror Life Is Theoretical. The Danger Is Anything But. With mirror life, scientists have given world leaders both the foresight and the time to address the danger. What's needed isn't alarm but action to ensure that mirror life remains just a footnote in human history&mdash;and ", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/mirror-life-is-theoretical-the-danger-is-anything-but.html'}, {'signal_id': '54a7beed2ea5126a', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': "OpenAI Says ChatGPT Is Safer for Teens. Now It Needs to Show Proof. Now, when OpenAI's system predicts that an account belongs to someone under 18, teen protections are automatically applied without waiting for a parent to activate them. But even ambitious efforts can fall short,", 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/openai-says-chatgpt-is-safer-for-teens-now-it-needs.html'}, {'signal_id': 'fefe734c50c0d8d9', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'Accelerating New Power Plants Depends on Better Data The United States is embarking on a vast build-out of its electric system. Transparent cost data would help regulators pinpoint avoidable delays, help developers assess risk, and help communities judge the value they are being ', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/accelerating-new-power-plants-depends-on-better-data.html'}, {'signal_id': '5581f5ab1400f06c', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The <em>Cyclospora</em> Outbreak Was a Warning: Q&amp;A with Saskia Popescu Saskia Popescu is an epidemiologist by training and a policy researcher at RAND. In this Q&amp;A, she discusses what the United States can do to prepare for future outbreaks like Cyclospora and other biol', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/the-cyclospora-outbreak-was-a-warning-qa-with-saskia.html'}, {'signal_id': '66a57de88708494d', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'The State of Public Education in 2026 in Five Charts RAND has spent more than a decade surveying educators across the United States and has expanded this effort to include the perspectives of students and parents. Among the hundreds of survey questions we fielded this past year, ', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/the-state-of-public-education-in-2026-in-five-charts.html'}, {'signal_id': 'cf978610d746d637', 'source': 'rand', 'text_snippet': 'AI, China, and the New Risks to U.S. Security: Q&amp;A with Matan Chorev Matan Chorev is vice president and director of RAND Global and Emerging Risks. In this Q&amp;A, he discusses some of the most consequential challenges facing the United States and the world.', 'url': 'https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2026/08/ai-china-and-the-new-risks-to-us-security-qa-with-matan.html'}, {'signal_id': '92f05a74e3d781af', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What could make AI self-regulation work? <p>For the new AI accord to work, industry self-regulation will need to be buttressed by binding enforcement or federal oversight.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-could-make-ai-self-regulation-work/', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-could-make-ai-self-regulation-work/'}, {'signal_id': 'eb386b2ee475b5b9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Investing in Europe’s next growth engine <p>With Western European investment becoming less dependable, Central and Eastern Europe faces a choice: attract new foreign capital, or do more to mobilize the investment potential within the region itself.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/investing-in-europes-next-growth-engine/'}, {'signal_id': 'cc82f1d42b60e03c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Chhangani quoted in Fortune on mBridge and dollar dominance <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-3/">Chhangani quoted in Fortune o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-3/'}, {'signal_id': '1f80f69b3684fd7b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Nikoladze quoted in a National Intelligence University monograph on the geoeconomic implications of the Israel-Hamas conflict <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'a4d2f09d0e258965', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Singh featured in Financial Times on Saudi Arabia’s withdrawal from mBridge <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-2/">Singh feature', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization-2/'}, {'signal_id': 'ab56aecbc49a4c80', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Putin aims to break Ukraine by terrorizing the civilian population <p>With the Russian army unable to defeat Ukraine on the battlefield, Putin is turning to terror tactics and is using ballistic missiles and jet drones in a bid to bomb Ukraine's civilian population into submissio", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-aims-to-break-ukraine-by-terrorizing-the-civilian-population/'}, {'signal_id': '0d99288883424895', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Can Mexico thread the needle between Washington and Beijing? <p>As US-Mexico trade talks approach, the Mexican government faces a delicate balancing act: curbing Chinese trade and investment without cutting off vital inputs and foreign capital.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://ww', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/can-mexico-thread-the-needle-between-washington-and-beijing/'}, {'signal_id': '81fe7c624c54ad06', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ports, power, and presence: How to defend Batanes from China <p>Manila and Washington should be proactive in preventing Chinese coercion or encroachment in the Philippines’ northern-most province.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/ports-power-and', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/ports-power-and-presence-how-to-defend-batanes-from-china/'}, {'signal_id': 'e2ee8c26a6bbbb77', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Resilience has a cost. So does complacency. <p>Gulf countries need to work together to build resilience, as they face new stresses from the Iran War.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/resilience-has-a-cost-so-does-complacency/">Resilience h', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/resilience-has-a-cost-so-does-complacency/'}, {'signal_id': 'd7f603093ce015cb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Making the EU’s new industrial rulebook work for Central Europe <p>As the EU rethinks its approach to industrial policy, Central Europe needs to make sure the shift strengthens the region’s manufacturing base.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econogr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/making-the-eus-new-industrial-rulebook-work-for-central-europe/'}, {'signal_id': '922e303338b5f50d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': '5 questions (and expert answers) about Bosnia and Herzegovina’s election <p>Atlantic Council experts explain the players, voting system, and implications for the EU and NATO. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/eye-on-europes-elections/5-quest', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/eye-on-europes-elections/5-questions-and-expert-answers-about-bosnia-and-herzegovinas-election/'}, {'signal_id': '956d875bcdd8b058', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukraine can play a key role enabling US energy exports to Europe <p>As Russia expands the bombardment of Ukraine’s civilian infrastructure, changes are taking place in the country's energy sector with implications for the United States and the future shape of European gas markets", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-can-play-a-key-role-enabling-us-energy-exports-to-europe/'}, {'signal_id': '8558e38c897320d2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Pfizer CEO Albert Bourla on AI and the future of medicine <p>Pfizer Chairman and CEO Albert Bourla joined Frederick Kempe to discuss how artificial intelligence is transforming the healthcare industry.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-wit', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/inflection-points-with-frederick-kempe/pfizer-ceo-albert-bourla-on-ai-and-the-future-of-medicine/'}, {'signal_id': 'c2ce9b93469f02be', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Brazil’s upcoming election is bigger than Lula or Bolsonaro <p>The congressional vote will be especially consequential for the balance of power facing the next administration.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/brazils-upcoming-election-is-bigger-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/brazils-upcoming-election-is-bigger-than-lula-or-bolsonaro/'}, {'signal_id': 'e1dd749336fca55c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Africa’s exit problem is the United States’ entry point <p>European and multilateral development finance institutions spent two decades backing funds that bought African companies. Those funds have aged, and their backers need distributions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.a', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/africasource/africas-exit-problem-is-the-united-states-entry-point/'}, {'signal_id': 'cdcd196b9b46411a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'To save its manufacturing base, Europe needs to look east <p>Europe is counting on Central and Eastern Europe to power its manufacturing revival—but first, it needs to make sure Germany’s slowdown doesn’t drag the region down with it.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlantic', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/to-save-its-manufacturing-base-europe-needs-to-look-east/'}, {'signal_id': 'f6a823bc7b108cec', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'US troops are leaving Iraq, but the US should stay <p>The end of Operation Inherent Resolve should not be the end of Washington\'s engagement with this important country in a region vital to US interests.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/us-troop', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/us-troops-are-leaving-iraq-but-the-us-should-stay/'}, {'signal_id': 'dfbea67b53721ca2', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'President Ahmed Al-Sharaa on Syria’s next chapter <p>Syrian President Ahmed Al-Sharaa joins the Atlantic Council to discuss Syria’s future and his government’s priorities for reconstruction, economic recovery, and institutional reform.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanti', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/president-ahmed-al-sharaa-on-syrias-next-chapter/'}, {'signal_id': '3a89434a74e76405', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Yes, transmission is dull. Read this article anyway. <p>Policymakers should prioritize electric power transmission to ensure the success of the US energy system.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/yes-transmission-is-dull-read-this-article', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/yes-transmission-is-dull-read-this-article-anyway/'}, {'signal_id': '2813b7ff80d8da7e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Europe needs a new strategy for Russian gray zone aggression <p>Europe needs a new counter-hybrid playbook, but an approach that focuses on coordinating responses after Russian attacks have already taken place is not an effective deterrent, write Maksym Beznosiuk and William Dixo', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/europe-needs-a-new-strategy-for-russian-grey-zone-aggression/'}, {'signal_id': 'de475a9642506ebb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s innovative robot offensive just reversed a year of Russian gains <p>Russian President Vladimir Putin’s hopes of capturing eastern Ukraine’s Donbas region have been dealt a major blow in recent months by an innovative Ukrainian offensive that has reversed over a year of ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-innovative-robot-offensive-just-reversed-a-year-of-russian-gains/'}, {'signal_id': 'f05668b8c44718a6', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Vladimir Putin only has two options in Ukraine: Total victory or endless war <p>US-led efforts to end the Russia-Ukraine War by offering the Kremlin limited territorial concessions reflect a fundamental misunderstanding of the imperial ambitions driving Putin's invasion, writes P", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/vladimir-putin-only-has-two-options-in-ukraine-total-victory-or-endless-war/'}, {'signal_id': '603d974542cc9b98', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Stopping Russia’s aggression requires holding its enablers accountable <p>Russia’s war is sustained by a network of enablers who supply weapons, labor, and sanctions-evasion channels.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/stopping-russias-aggression-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/stopping-russias-aggression-requires-holding-its-enablers-accountable/'}, {'signal_id': '7ebba46ec4c250b7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The strategic rationale for closer investment ties between Europe and the Gulf <p>Europe and the Gulf both stand to benefit from investing more in each region. Which projects make the most sense?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/i', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-strategic-rationale-for-closer-investment-ties-between-europe-and-the-gulf/'}, {'signal_id': '36a45033654cfb5d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Trade and connectivity in the Europe-Gulf strategic partnership <p>Boosting trade between European and Gulf states requires progress on two key projects planned to connect the regions: the India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor, and a free trade agreement. Can the disruption ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/trade-and-connectivity-in-the-europe-gulf-strategic-partnership/'}, {'signal_id': '4979f250c1fdc327', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Three principles to guide European-Gulf defense cooperation <p>How can Europe and Gulf cooperate more effectively on defense?</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/three-principles-to-guide-european-gulf-defense-cooperation', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/three-principles-to-guide-european-gulf-defense-cooperation/'}, {'signal_id': '625be02f4fcb0aab', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "How Europe and the Gulf can unite behind an energy-transition agenda <p>European and Gulf states share a strong interest in restoring the free flow of energy cut off by the Iran war, and in reducing their economies' exposure to chokepoints like the Strait of Hormuz. What's their ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/how-europe-and-the-gulf-can-unite-behind-an-energy-transition-agenda/'}, {'signal_id': '790ced5b25834411', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in POLITICO on the cost of Russia’s hybrid war on European businesses <p>On September 29, Elisabeth Braw was published in POLITICO on the financial costs of Russia&#8217;s gray-zone aggression.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-polit', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-politico-on-the-cost-of-russias-hybrid-war-on-european-businesses/'}, {'signal_id': '599f4fd607e28c44', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Don’t ignore the ‘dead rats’ of global disorder <p>A war historian’s recent essay underscores the urgency of addressing the issues increasing strife around the world today. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dont-ignore-the-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/dont-ignore-the-dead-rats-of-global-disorder/'}, {'signal_id': '8fdb22b72aea317f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'For better or for worse, NATO’s future could define Trump’s foreign policy legacy <p>The Pentagon’s review of US force posture in Europe have high stakes for the United States and the president himself.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-bette', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/for-better-or-for-worse-natos-future-could-define-trumps-foreign-policy-legacy/'}, {'signal_id': '7d64f8b570969ece', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What’s behind the Algeria-UAE rupture <p>Algeria\'s severing of diplomatic ties with the UAE reflects a broader struggle over regional influence and sovereignty.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/whats-behind-the-algeria-uae-rupture/">What’s', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/whats-behind-the-algeria-uae-rupture/'}, {'signal_id': '0a53cb72535892ec', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Technology and the Global South: A US strategy for competitiveness <p>The United States and China are engaged in a strategic competition for scientific and technological leadership. To prevail, the United States must strengthen its tech-centric engagement with countries across th', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/technology-and-the-global-south-a-us-strategy-for-competitiveness/'}, {'signal_id': 'ac2eb7a8d5e401b7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The IMF’s big test in Bangkok <p>The IMF is heading to Bangkok with plenty on its plate. From China’s industrial policy to US fiscal deficits and Europe’s economic challenges, the annual meetings will put the Fund’s global mandate in the spotlight.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-imfs-big-test-in-bangkok/'}, {'signal_id': 'adbf313eb13412a9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in Sky News on the safety of UK air bases <p>On September 28, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed by Sky News to discuss the Fairford Plot, and the safety of UK air bases.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-sky-news-on-the-safety-of-uk-air', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-sky-news-on-the-safety-of-uk-air-bases/'}, {'signal_id': '56755e10530399a8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in The Spectator on the West’s readiness for an undersea war <p>On September 26, Elisabeth Braw was published in The Spectator in an article discussing the West&#8217;s preparedness for an undersea war.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-the-spectator-on-the-wests-readiness-for-an-undersea-war/'}, {'signal_id': '045f11664a5c1c30', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from New York: Latin America has opened a new chapter with Washington <p>The diplomacy around this year’s United Nations General Assembly showcased new initiative in the Americas to increase economic growth and tackle crime.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-new-york-latin-america-has-opened-a-new-chapter-with-washington/'}, {'signal_id': '3fa1823f98f113f8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What did (and didn’t) happen at the Trump-Xi summit <p>What the latest Trump-Xi summit changed, left unresolved, and what to watch before they meet again.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-did-and-didnt-happen-at-the-trump-x', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-did-and-didnt-happen-at-the-trump-xi-summit/'}, {'signal_id': '7c4bf79dee87933b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for The National Interest: Donald Trump’s New York State of Mind <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-donald-trumps-new-york-state-of-mind/">Charai for The National Interest: Donald Trump’s New Yor', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-national-interest-donald-trumps-new-york-state-of-mind/'}, {'signal_id': '9083cce67e1efa53', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The Saudi economy can hold out through year’s end—even if oil exports drop to zero <p>First the Strait of Hormuz closed, so Saudi Arabia started sending more oil over land through its East-West Pipeline. Then drone strikes damaged the pipeline, and the Iran-backed Houthis fired m', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/the-saudi-economy-can-hold-out-through-years-end-even-if-oil-exports-drop-to-zero/'}, {'signal_id': '31bd7ea4e0556b38', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine’s defense tech sector must offer investors more than innovation <p>Since the start of Russia’s full-scale invasion in 2022, Ukraine has built one of the world’s most dynamic defense tech ecosystems under conditions few industries ever face. However, innovation alone will ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraines-defense-tech-sector-must-offer-investors-more-than-innovation/'}, {'signal_id': '3971b7965f074384', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in Sky News on a National Resilience Corps for the UK <p>On September 24, Elisabeth Braw was interviewed on Sky News to discuss the possibility of forming a national resilience corps for the UK.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-sky-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-sky-news-on-a-national-resilience-corps-for-the-uk/'}, {'signal_id': 'bef2fb620564d64b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in Foreign Policy on the Far Right’s Threat to the Laws of the Sea <p>On September 24, Elisabeth Braw was published in Foreign Policy in an article on how the far right wants to abandon stranded seafarers.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/b', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-foreign-policy-on-the-far-rights-threat-to-the-laws-of-the-sea/'}, {'signal_id': '2c8618c2243d02e8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Full transcript: The 2026 Atlantic Council Global Citizen Awards honor four leaders seeking to improve the state of the world <p>The star-studded evening celebrated the achievements of four global citizens who are using partnership and inspiration to shape what comes next for the', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/news/transcripts/full-transcript-the-2026-atlantic-council-global-citizen-awards-honor-four-leaders-seeking-to-improve-the-state-of-the-world/'}, {'signal_id': 'bd51343c62884209', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The 2026 Global Citizen Awards: Celebrating leadership that builds what comes next <p>The Atlantic Council honored the Finnish president, the Australian prime minister, the president and CEO of Formula 1, and a celebrated actress, singer, and producer.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="ht', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/event-recap/the-2026-global-citizen-awards-celebrating-leadership-that-builds-what-comes-next/'}, {'signal_id': '79cfbf8986c667a0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin’s Ukraine invasion has made Russia China’s junior partner <p>Putin’s evident inability to secure Beijing’s backing for the Power of Siberia-2 pipeline is strengthening international perceptions that the invasion of Ukraine has reduced Russia to the status of China’s junior ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putins-ukraine-invasion-has-made-russia-chinas-junior-partner/'}, {'signal_id': '2280097e0be8e3fb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Building a multilateral cognitive warfare defense network: A collaborative framework for the United States, Japan, and Taiwan <p>Beijing is pressuring Japan, South Korea, Taiwan, and the Philippines not only with ships and aircraft but also in the cognitive domain—which no multil', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/building-a-multilateral-cognitive-warfare-defense-network/'}, {'signal_id': '6ac73bd3ca58a1c7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Three things to know about Trump’s Greenland deal <p>The agreement signed on the sidelines of the United Nations General Assembly makes several important changes to the status quo.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/three-things-to-know-about-trum', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/three-things-to-know-about-trumps-greenland-deal/'}, {'signal_id': 'b1275cb947e3a5eb', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'America is not ready for the drone threat <p>Counter-drone technology is not enough to address the threat to US critical infrastructure.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/america-is-not-ready-for-the-drone-threat/">America is not ready for the dr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/america-is-not-ready-for-the-drone-threat/'}, {'signal_id': 'f70be57b80c9013b', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'A diesel export ban could disrupt US supply chains <p>There are second- and third-order consequences of a ban to consider, including what it would mean for Latin American countries.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/a-diesel-export-ban-could-disr', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/a-diesel-export-ban-could-disrupt-us-supply-chains/'}, {'signal_id': '6715729c491ef92a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AI data under the microscope: Accelerating and securing the AI data supply chain for the health and biopharmaceutical sectors <p>This report examines how health and biopharmaceutical companies interact with the data components of the AI supply chain, and how a fractured global re', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/report/ai-data-under-the-microscope-accelerating-and-securing-the-ai-data-supply-chain-for-the-health-and-biopharmaceutical-sectors/'}, {'signal_id': '0e23fa2e9bd120c0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Ukrainians are braced for a brutal winter. Are the Russians also ready? <p>With Ukraine's air defenses running low, Russia is expected to escalate the bombardment of Ukrainian cities and civilian infrastructure ahead of the coming winter season in a bid to freeze the country into", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukrainians-are-braced-for-a-brutal-winter-are-the-russians-also-ready/'}, {'signal_id': '5b647d8a44f2e445', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Strait talk: Yemen, mercenaries and the Iran war <p>In this first video episode of the podcast, Alia is joined by Ibrahim Jalal, an expert on Yemen and the Gulf. Ibrahim describes the major military escalation unfolding along the Red Sea coast and the tactics used by the Houthis.', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/podcast/strait-talk-yemen-mercenaries-and-the-iran-war/'}, {'signal_id': '8b03b9dde55a8812', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'To achieve its next economic leap, Vietnam needs to move beyond the factory floor <p>Vietnam’s export-driven growth has been remarkable. But with domestic firms capturing relatively little of the value, Hanoi now needs to turn foreign investment into broader gains at home.</p>\n<p', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/to-achieve-its-next-economic-leap-vietnam-needs-to-move-beyond-the-factory-floor/'}, {'signal_id': '3580482a0c854d1f', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Matthew Bryza joins Azerbaijan’s ARB TV 24 about new transport corridor investments helping to bolster peace between Azerbaijan and Armenia <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/matthew-bryza-joins-azerbaijans-arb-tv-24-about-new-transpor', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/matthew-bryza-joins-azerbaijans-arb-tv-24-about-new-transport-corridor-investments-helping-to-bolster-peace-between-azerbaijan-and-armenia/'}, {'signal_id': 'f88d6d6a937835b0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Atlantic Council Launches Power of Sports Center to Harness Sports as Platform for Diplomacy, Innovation, Economic Growth, and Global Cooperation <p>NEW YORK, SEPTEMBER 22, 2026 – The Atlantic Council today announced the launch of its Power of Sports Center, a groundbreaking conv', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/news/press-releases/atlantic-council-launches-power-of-sports-center-to-harness-sports-as-platform-for-diplomacy-innovation-economic-growth-and-global-cooperation/'}, {'signal_id': '616782a7b85d3067', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Youth sports can help African countries build a legacy of champions <p>African countries possess plenty of raw sporting talent. But replicable success is produced by systems.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/youth-sports-can-help-african-countri', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/youth-sports-can-help-african-countries-build-a-legacy-of-champions/'}, {'signal_id': 'eb08157ba8fc613c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What to expect at the Trump-Xi summit in Washington <p>The success of the meeting will likely hinge on just a few important issues, including artificial intelligence safety, Taiwan, and trade.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-to-expect-at-t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-to-expect-at-the-trump-xi-summit-in-washington/'}, {'signal_id': '6a53dddc78772777', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The four issues our experts are watching ahead of this week’s Trump-Xi summit <p>From AI governance to trade and economic headwinds in Beijing, our experts break down the key questions shaping the summit—and what could come next.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcounc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-four-issues-our-experts-are-watching-ahead-of-this-weeks-trump-xi-summit/'}, {'signal_id': '66ef42dca5177d4a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'AI is sprinting past human control. Can testing and evaluation catch up? <p>Frontier AI is exposing the limits of today\'s testing systems. The United States needs a national AI assurance ecosystem.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/ai-is-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/geotech-cues/ai-is-sprinting-past-human-control-can-testing-and-evaluation-catch-up/'}, {'signal_id': '74671cd3ba398509', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The Syria policy the US got wrong—and the bittersweet moment Washington finally got right <p>A former State Department official dissects how the US helped defeat ISIS but didn\'t protect the Syrian people.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/the-syria-policy-the-us-got-wrong-and-the-bittersweet-moment-washington-finally-got-right/'}, {'signal_id': '3a71a259cdfe28c9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Baku: Azerbaijan must look forward even amid Russian and Iranian conflicts <p>A recent visit to the Caucasus region reveals a country exposed to two wars, but also one that must not wait to chart its economic and diplomatic future.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://w', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-baku-azerbaijan-must-look-forward-even-amid-russian-and-iranian-conflicts/'}, {'signal_id': 'ede89cb32ded5d21', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Don’t talk about optimism in Syria, talk about action <p>It’s been twenty months since Bashar al-Assad’s fall. People expect more, and patience is wearing thin.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/dont-talk-about-optimisim-in-syria-talk-about', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/dont-talk-about-optimisim-in-syria-talk-about-action/'}, {'signal_id': 'ee7a7a93859dd45a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'In Amwaj media, Matthew Bryza comments on the Mecca Agreement and the question of it extending to the South Caucuses <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/in-amwaj-media-matthew-bryza-comments-on-the-mecca-agreement-and-the-question-of-it', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/in-amwaj-media-matthew-bryza-comments-on-the-mecca-agreement-and-the-question-of-it-extending-to-the-south-caucuses/'}, {'signal_id': '6c0f4833192051f9', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the Greenland deal means for the transatlantic alliance <p>Our experts unpack what we know and what to expect from the announced security deal involving the US, Denmark, and Greenland.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/fastthinking/what-the-greenland-deal-means-for-the-transatlantic-alliance/'}, {'signal_id': 'b051929a24350dd0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Charai for the Jerusalem Strategic Tribune: The Muslim Brotherhood: Follow the Money <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-muslim-brotherhood-follow-the-money/">Charai for the Jerusalem Strat', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/charai-for-the-jerusalem-strategic-tribune-the-muslim-brotherhood-follow-the-money/'}, {'signal_id': 'bb16e37fc33f7fdf', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Tannebaum quoted in the New York Times on US unreliability influencing de-dollarization efforts <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/tannebaum-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-us-unreliability-influencing-de-dollarization-efforts/'}, {'signal_id': 'c654acb51a3121f1', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Lipsky quoted in the New York Times on the prospects of de-dollarization <p>Read the full article here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization/">Lipsky quoted in t', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/lipsky-quoted-in-the-new-york-times-on-the-prospects-of-de-dollarization/'}, {'signal_id': '0cdfe08fd5115f1d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Goldsmith Romero interviewed on CNN about the rise in prediction market trading <p>Watch the full interview here</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goldsmith-romero-interviewed-on-cnn-about-the-rise-in-prediction-market-trading/">G', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/goldsmith-romero-interviewed-on-cnn-about-the-rise-in-prediction-market-trading/'}, {'signal_id': 'a5f72942aa977575', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Fortifying USMCA through US–Mexico investment screening coordination <p>One of the biggest blind spots in the US-Mexico-Canada trade agreement is its treatment of capital and foreign investment screening. The current review presents an opportunity to address this and build a safe', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/issue-brief/fortifying-usmca-through-us-mexico-investment-screening-coordination/'}, {'signal_id': 'ec8be4d1636c88de', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ukraine can do more to counter Russia’s illicit finance threat <p>For more than four years, Ukraine has impressed global audiences with the country’s ability to defend itself against Russia on land, at sea, and in the air. Illicit finance is another important front in the fight a', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/ukraine-can-do-more-to-counter-russias-illicit-finance-threat/'}, {'signal_id': '23a1e8f57b08c4f5', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What von der Leyen’s SOTU speech got right about energy—and where the EU still needs to pivot <p>The EU State of the Union address recognizes important energy system challenges but also leaves details on actions murky.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blog', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/energysource/what-von-der-leyens-sotu-speech-got-right-about-energy-and-where-the-eu-still-needs-to-pivot/'}, {'signal_id': '80b58aa71c14e811', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Putin is escalating against NATO but a Baltic incursion remains unlikely <p>The recent escalation in Russian gray zone aggression across Europe has sparked a lively debate over how far the Kremlin may be prepared to go, but a Russian attack on the Baltic states remains unlikely, ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/putin-is-escalating-against-nato-but-a-baltic-incursion-remains-unlikely/'}, {'signal_id': 'c0463aee1f611401', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Macron won the argument over European strategic autonomy. Will better European defense come of it? <p>Delivering real capabilities is where this vision of strategic autonomy will succeed or fail.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/macron-won-the-a', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/macron-won-the-argument-over-european-strategic-autonomy-will-better-european-defense-come-of-it/'}, {'signal_id': '0750f955abe48c14', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Ten years into Trump’s trade experiment, the US continues to defy expectations <p>A decade of tariffs and trade wars has yet to deliver the economic collapse many critics predicted. Instead, the data tell a more complicated story.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcoun', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/ten-years-into-trumps-trade-experiment-the-us-continues-to-defy-expectations/'}, {'signal_id': '43f461da4d9ac9a8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in BFBS on the importance of undersea cables <p>On September 17, Elisabeth Braw was quoted in BFBS in an article on the growing threat to the global maritime order.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-bfbs-on-the-importance-of-undersea', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-bfbs-on-the-importance-of-undersea-cables/'}, {'signal_id': '533c51c87ebd0fa8', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Rich Outzen appears on Saudi Arabia’s AlHadath, discussing space militarization threats from Russia and China, and the US commitment to the Outer Space Treaty of 1967 <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/rich-outzen-appears-on-saudi-arab', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/rich-outzen-appears-on-saudi-arabias-alhadath-discussing-space-militarization-threats-from-russia-and-china-and-the-us-commitment-to-the-outer-space-treaty-of-1967/'}, {'signal_id': '8c5613ad2396025a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'In Al-Monitor, Yevgeniya Gaber comments on the Black Sea security architecture, saying closer coordination among the region’s NATO members are all the more important <p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/yevgeniya-gaber-comments-on-the-bl', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/insight-impact/in-the-news/yevgeniya-gaber-comments-on-the-black-sea-security-architecture-saying-closer-coordination-among-the-regions-nato-members-are-all-the-more-important/'}, {'signal_id': 'dc3fb86641600f3e', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'New voices, old friends: How Russia targets its messaging in the Global South <p>The latest report in the Atlantic Council\'s Russia Tomorrow series examines the themes and methods that Russia uses to target audiences in the Global South.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlan', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/russia-tomorrow/how-russia-targets-is-messaging-in-the-global-south/'}, {'signal_id': '9def8f6c6303dbe7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The Graham sanctions act is a chance to punish Putin. Here’s what the White House should do next. <p>The just-passed Graham Sanctioning Russia and Iran Act is a victory for Ukraine and the bipartisan coalition backing it.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/d', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-graham-sanctions-act-is-a-chance-to-punish-putin-heres-what-the-white-house-should-do-next/'}, {'signal_id': 'e3af7fe28bbaeece', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What von der Leyen and Carney are up to with Canada’s ‘associate’ EU membership <p>In her state of the union address, the European Commission president proposed Ottawa join the European Union, but not as a full member.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/disp', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-von-der-leyen-and-carney-are-up-to-with-canadas-associate-eu-membership/'}, {'signal_id': '11a863cdef9d5595', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The White House has an AI oversight plan. But who will do the overseeing? <p>A third-party AI auditing market could help close federal oversight gaps and complement the new White House\'s new rules. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-white-hou', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/the-white-house-has-an-ai-oversight-plan-but-who-will-do-the-overseeing/'}, {'signal_id': '17e0b012102f9136', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Could the GCC and Iran collaborate to solve the Strait of Hormuz crisis? <p>A Gulf-led maritime cooperation could break the Hormuz stalemate by offering Iran an off-ramp while preventing unilateral control.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/could-the-gcc-and-iran-collaborate-to-solve-the-strait-of-hormuz-crisis/'}, {'signal_id': '36706f032fa650c0', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'With Putin overextended in Ukraine, Armenia is turning away from Russia <p>Every day Ukraine keeps fighting, Russian influence grows weaker in the countries of the ex-USSR that Moscow refers to as the “near abroad.” Nowhere is this Russian retreat clearer than in Armenia, writes ', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/with-putin-overextended-in-ukraine-armenia-is-turning-away-from-russia/'}, {'signal_id': 'a0fb2461d5aa1199', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Dispatch from Seoul: How Asian allies can help the US with Iran <p>Allies in the Asia-Pacific should recognize that they cannot continue to be perceived as unwilling to assist the US in its conflict with Iran.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/di', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dispatch-from-seoul-how-asian-allies-can-help-the-us-with-iran/'}, {'signal_id': 'fabd9c0f08551812', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'The Philippines needs to turn fast growth into productive growth <p>The Southeast Asian nation has proved it can grow. Now, amid shifting supply chains and rising geopolitical tensions, it must prove it can grow more productively.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcoun', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/the-philippines-needs-to-turn-fast-growth-into-productive-growth/'}, {'signal_id': '3f30bacec417376d', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Can oil deals reset US-Iraqi relations? <p>Iraq has a short window of time to rein in its militias and create favorable commercial conditions to improve ties with the US.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/can-oil-deals-reset-us-iraqi-relati', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/menasource/can-oil-deals-reset-us-iraqi-relations/'}, {'signal_id': '57a74ab4f872fbdc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Democracy is losing ground. The economic case for it is not. <p>While overall democracy has deteriorated globally in recent years, countries that democratize still see greater economic growth and prosperity over time.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispa', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/democracy-is-losing-ground-the-economic-case-for-it-is-not/'}, {'signal_id': '668389056ca8977a', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Digital sovereignty and Europe’s democracy stack:\xa0Delivering on the European Union’s priorities for the 2028–2034 Multiannual Financial Framework <p>The EU's digital sovereignty agenda is missing a funded, independent institutional capability to hold its own technology investment", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blog-post/digital-sovereignty-and-europes-democracy-stack/'}, {'signal_id': '44704d31289da1bc', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in Wall Street Journal on Irish security <p>On September 15, Elisabeth Braw was quoted in the Wall Street Journal in an article on Russia&#8217;s shadow fleet using Irish waters to bypass NATO security.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-wall-street-journal-on-irish-security/'}, {'signal_id': 'adbce8e5c47323e7', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Don’t count on Trump and Xi to slow down AI. Don’t count them out either. <p>Concerns about catastrophic risks to humanity have put artificial intelligence at the top of the agenda for the leaders’ upcoming meeting.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/dont-count-on-trump-and-xi-to-slow-down-ai-dont-count-them-out-either/'}, {'signal_id': '1382aa09f8589a76', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': '2026 Atlantic Council Global Citizen Awards to Honor Finnish President, Australian Prime Minister, Formula One President and CEO, and Actress and Musician Cynthia Erivo <p>NEW YORK, SEPTEMBER 14, 2026 – The Atlantic Council announced today that its fifteenth annual Atlantic Counc', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/news/press-releases/2026-atlantic-council-global-citizen-awards-to-honor-finnish-president-australian-prime-minister-formula-one-president-and-ceo-and-actress-and-musician-cynthia-erivo/'}, {'signal_id': '11dbb2e696438627', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Beyond the Reaper: Rethinking the future of multirole drones <p>The US Air Force should consider spreading the multirole model across networks of smaller, cheaper drones.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/beyond-the-reaper-rethinking-the-future-o', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/beyond-the-reaper-rethinking-the-future-of-multirole-drones/'}, {'signal_id': 'bd24ee54cdf07869', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Friends with few trade benefits <p>Free trade agreements were supposed to protect US trading partners. But the Trump administration’s tariffs are putting that promise to the test.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/friends-with-few-trade-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/econographics/friends-with-few-trade-benefits/'}, {'signal_id': 'db04fe594c8f8810', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Braw in BFBS on the Russian activity in Svalbard <p>On September 14, Elisabeth Braw was quoted in BFBS on the strategic importance of Svalbard, and Russia&#8217;s increasing action near the archipelago.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-b', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/commentary/braw-in-bfbs-on-the-russian-activity-in-svalbard/'}, {'signal_id': '41397d46575910b3', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Three African economies show how China’s slowdown is reshaping trade <p>From Angolan oil to Congolese copper, China\'s economic slowdown is creating new winners and losers across Africa.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/three-african-economies-sh', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/three-african-economies-show-how-chinas-slowdown-is-reshaping-trade/'}, {'signal_id': 'f7086f7577420b06', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Trump and Xi should rethink how to run the AI race <p>The threat of frontier artificial intelligence must be at the top of the agenda for the upcoming meeting between the leaders.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-and-', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/content-series/inflection-points/trump-and-xi-should-rethink-how-to-run-the-ai-race/'}, {'signal_id': '3296f68c704be87c', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What the proposed AI slowdown means for the US, China, and humanity\xa0at large <p>Atlantic Council experts assess the new commitments from the leaders of Anthropic, OpenAI, and others, along with the state of the tech and the risk to the human race. </p>\n<p>The post <a href="https:', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-the-proposed-ai-slowdown-means-for-the-us-china-and-humanity-at-large/'}, {'signal_id': 'b1f8871cd29f1946', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'Learning from Ukraine’s unrivaled experience of Russian cyber warfare <p>No country in the world today knows more about Russian cyber warfare than Ukraine, but further steps are required in order to help Kyiv’s partners make the most of Ukraine’s unrivaled experience, writes Iryn', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/blogs/ukrainealert/learning-from-ukraines-unrivaled-experience-of-russian-cyber-warfare/'}, {'signal_id': 'c771ce3dfa139a15', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': "Submission to the UN: Advancing the just repatriation of illicit funds <p>How can the UN and the international community ensure that when illicit funds are seized, victims of the illicit activity benefit? The Atlantic Council's Strategic Litigation Program contributed a brief to ", 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/in-depth-research-reports/submission-to-the-un-advancing-the-just-repatriation-of-illicit-funds/'}, {'signal_id': 'd57c441024fb9a03', 'source': 'atlantic_council', 'text_snippet': 'What Rubio’s Latin America tour means for Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru <p>Experts look at what Rubio\'s tour signals about the US push for closer cooperation with Latin America\'s new crop of conservatives.</p>\n<p>The post <a href="https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-rub', 'url': 'https://www.atlanticcouncil.org/dispatches/what-rubios-tour-means-for-colombia-ecuador-and-peru/'}, {'signal_id': '71095b01cc9b7523', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'China-linked hackers posed as former US officials, Anthropic employee to target AI experts Proofpoint identified phishing campaigns that borrowed prominent figures’ identities to approach U.S. policy researchers before attempting to steal access to their cloud accounts.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/10/china-linked-hackers-posed-former-us-officials-anthropic-employee-target-ai-experts/416384/'}, {'signal_id': '32cdeb177c9ba7fc', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Hegseth plans ‘Autonomous Warfare Command’ The military’s 12th combatant command was among a slew of announcements in a Quantico speech Wednesday.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/policy/2026/09/hegseth-plans-autonomous-warfare-command/416358/'}, {'signal_id': 'fd0683ab47d99e93', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Defense Business Brief: End-of-fiscal-year advice for founders; Navy drone boats; Powerus to go public', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/business/2026/09/defense-business-brief-end-fiscal-year-advice-founders-navy-drone-boats-powerus-go-public/416357/'}, {'signal_id': '8001ac77f3a179cb', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Pentagon update on National Defense Strategy cites progress, omits key threats The report to Congress  notes accomplishments but masks depleted arsenals, strategic distractions, and a quiet retreat from European defense.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/threats/2026/09/pentagon-update-national-defense-strategy-cites-progress-omits-key-threats/416329/'}, {'signal_id': 'f83ed6d4ac01b312', 'source': 'defense_one', 'text_snippet': 'Army awards counterdrone contracts worth more than $4B But there’s room for more—up to $7 billion.', 'url': 'https://www.defenseone.com/business/2026/09/army-awards-more-4-billion-counterdrone-contracts-putting-pentagons-new-drone-marketplace-test/416327/'}, {'signal_id': 'e6fe34f1f8481da3', 'source': 'defense_one', '